<p class="eyebrow">Search foundations</p><h1>Make your important pages easier to discover</h1><p class="lead">A technical SEO review identifies observable barriers across a defined set of pages. Recommendations include evidence, affected URLs and a practical next step.</p><div class="grid"><article class="card"><h2>Metadata and indexability</h2><p>Review titles, descriptions, canonical destinations and robots directives on agreed landing pages.</p></article><article class="card"><h2>Internal navigation</h2><p>Check whether important destinations can be reached, and flag missing or unexpected links.</p></article><article class="card"><h2>Clear handover</h2><p>Receive a prioritized issue register that separates observed defects from items requiring further investigation.</p></article></div><section><h2>What the review does not promise</h2><p>Search engines control indexing and rankings. A technical check does not establish search performance, and recommendations do not guarantee increased traffic.</p><p>Content strategy, backlink acquisition and ongoing implementation require a separate agreement.</p><a class="button" href="/contact">Discuss a focused review</a><p>Return to <a href="/services">all services</a>.</p></section>
</Base>
